BSI's advisory WID-SEC-2026-1435 lists the two pfSense CE flaws as critical but says nothing about patch status or mitigation, so the critical-unpatched framing and the claim that a national authority recommends mitigation go. CVE-2025-69690 scores 9.1 in ENISA's EUVD against the researcher's 8.8, both flaws need administrator credentials, Netgate's no-patch position comes from the researcher, and the supplier disputes both in the CVE records; no source addresses pfSense Plus.
